<h2>AI 2040: Plan A — the &ldquo;positive scenario&rdquo; that says delay superintelligence until 2040 (overview)</h2>
<p>The AI Futures Project, known for <strong>AI 2027</strong>, has published its follow-up, <strong>&ldquo;AI 2040: Plan A&rdquo;</strong>. This document is not a <strong>prediction</strong> of the future but a <strong>normative scenario (a recommendation)</strong> that says <em>&ldquo;this is what we would like to see happen.&rdquo;</em> If AI 2027 painted the ending of the superintelligence race as <strong>human extinction or an irreversible concentration of power</strong>, Plan A is the <strong>alternative the same authors put forward saying &ldquo;let us do this instead.&rdquo;</strong> This article is not a verbatim rendering of the original but a <strong>commentary</strong> compiled by cross-checking public summaries, press reports and author comments, and it is the first installment (overview and hub) of the <strong>four-part series</strong> in this folder.</p>

